  "_doc": "The campaign chain (DECISIONS T-033): Map 0 -> Map 1 -> Map 2. Each map's own json carries its 'exfil' block (round, target, beacon position, window); this table holds what is shared: the scene for every map id, the arrival rules on a new map, the vote/skip tuning, and the two transition cutscenes (shots are data: camera from/to/look in the departing map's frame, seconds, VO ids, effects). A map whose scene is missing ends the run on a 'campaign continues' screen with the profile updated. standalone: built levels playable from the launcher that are not in the chain yet (UPDATE 07: Map 4's acts land here one by one and move into the chain with the boarding step); MapCatalog lists them so they bake map data and are checked like the rest. UPDATE 07 (T-108): the chain continues past Totenhafen into Map 4 'Fernflug' as four act scenes (map04a..d); Morgenrot (map03, design-only) slots between map02_totenhafen and map04a_thalbach when it is built (its exfil would replace map02's). `standalone`: built levels playable from the launcher before they join the chain. `arrival_kits`: what a launcher 'skip to Act n' start carries (Campaign.begin_at).",
